{
  "Name": "Windows Escalate UAC Protection Bypass (Via SilentCleanup)",
  "Description": "There's a task in Windows Task Scheduler called \"SilentCleanup\" which, while it's executed as Users, automatically runs with elevated privileges. When it runs, it executes the file %windir%\\system32\\cleanmgr.exe. Since it runs as Users, and we can control user's environment variables, %windir% (normally pointing to C:\\Windows) can be changed to point to whatever we want, and it'll run as admin.",
